From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DE25-Nano Port <de25-nano@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Keep DE25 core switch under systemd

The original MiSTer restart path double-forks because the DE10-Nano launches
Main outside a service manager. On DE25-Nano, systemd owns Main and interprets
the parent exit as a service failure, potentially starting another instance
while the detached successor is active. Replace the process in place on this
platform so systemd continues tracking the selected core.
---
 fpga_io.cpp | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/fpga_io.cpp b/fpga_io.cpp
index 0fb4efe..1d59b68 100644
--- a/fpga_io.cpp
+++ b/fpga_io.cpp
@@ -886,6 +886,13 @@ void app_restart(const char *path, const char *xml, const char *exe)
 	const char *appname = exe ? exe : getappname();
 	printf("restarting to %s\n", appname);
 
+#ifdef MISTER_DE25
+	// systemd owns the DE25 Main process. Preserve its PID across a core
+	// switch so Restart=always cannot launch a competing second instance.
+	execl(appname, appname, path, xml, NULL);
+	printf("Something went wrong. Rebooting...\n");
+	reboot(1);
+#else
 	//a cleaner way to re-start
 	pid_t child = fork();
 	if (child > 0) _exit(0);
@@ -898,6 +905,7 @@ void app_restart(const char *path, const char *xml, const char *exe)
 	printf("Something went wrong. Rebooting...\n");
 	reboot(1);
 	_exit(1);
+#endif
 }
 
 void fpga_core_reset(int reset)
